UPDATE companies SET description='H & H Custom Metal Fabricating, Inc. was founded in 1996 in Plaistow, New Hampshire, just over the Massachusetts border. The company is family-owned and operated, focusing on custom metal fabrication for a variety of industries.

The shop specializes in unique, complex fabrications using aluminum, black iron, copper, shaped steel, and stainless steel. Welding services cover TIG, MIG, arc, oxy-acetylene, spot, plasma cutting, portable on-site welding, soldering, and cast iron welding. The company stocks large quantities of material to enable quick turnaround.

H & H serves a broad range of industries in the New England area, with explicit experience in medical and hospital equipment as well as food processing (e.g., conveyors).

The company emphasizes design assistance to find the most cost-effective process, a well-equipped facility with large-capacity equipment such as a plasma table and automated punching, and on-site welding services. It is fully insured and highlights its family-owned structure as a basis for personalized customer service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shearing", "Punching", "Bending", "Rolling", "Sawing", "Automated Punching", "Drilling", "Plasma Cutting", "Design and Manufacturing", "Machine Parts", "Forming", "Design Assistance", "TIG Welding", "MIG Welding", "Arc Welding", "Oxy Acetylene Welding", "Spot Welding", "Portable On-Site Welding", "Soldering", "Cast Iron Welding"], "industries": ["Medical/Hospital", "Food Processing"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Black Iron", "Copper", "Shaped Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Delrin", "Polycarbonate"], "equipment": ["Plasma Table", "Automated Punching"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design assistance for cost-effective processes", "Well-equipped shop with large-capacity equipment (plasma table, automated punching)", "Quick turnaround via stocked inventory", "On-site and off-site welding services", "Family-owned with focus on personalized customer service"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Plaistow, NH -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Capabilities: shearing, punching, bending, rolling, sawing, automated punching, drilling, plasma cutting, design and manufacturing, machining, forming, design assistance -> /about", "Welding capabilities: TIG, MIG, arc, oxy-acetylene, spot, plasma cutting, portable on-site, soldering, cast iron -> /about", "Materials: aluminum, black iron, copper, shaped steel, stainless steel -> /", "Materials: Delrin, Polycarbonate -> db (capabilities array)", "Industries: Medical/Hospital -> db (industries_served)", "Food processing conveyor example -> /about", "Quick turnaround via stocked inventory -> /about", "On-site welding services -> /about", "Design assistance for cost-effective processes -> /about", "Fully insured -> /about", "Plasma Table equipment -> /about", "Automated Punching equipment -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "H.H. Custom Metal Fabricating, Inc. specializes in unique, complex fabrications with a wide variety of products fabricated from materials to finished products.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='h-h-custom-metal-fabricating' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='H&H Classic Parts was founded in 1987 in Bentonville, Arkansas, as a family-owned business.

The company operates as a major online retailer of classic Chevrolet and GMC restoration parts, maintaining an inventory of over 25,000 items covering vehicles from 1955 through 1987. The catalog spans structural components such as quarter panels and floor pans, trim, weatherstripping, wiring harnesses, and modern upgrades including hidden radio systems and vintage-style air conditioning units. A technical support team staffed by experienced restorers assists customers with fitment, installation, and part selection.

H&H Classic Parts serves classic Chevrolet and GMC enthusiasts, from first-time restorers to seasoned professionals, supplying parts for models such as C10/C20 pickups, Impala, Bel Air, Chevelle, Camaro, and Nova. The company ships orders across the United States and internationally, building a loyal customer base that returns for multiple restoration projects.

The business was started to combine passion with professionalism, offering enthusiast-level expertise alongside competitive pricing and rapid fulfillment. The founders emphasize that their personal restoration experience informs every customer interaction, ensuring that technical guidance reflects hands-on knowledge of the parts they sell.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Classic Chevrolet and GMC parts distribution", "Technical restoration support", "Fast order fulfillment and shipping", "Quality assurance (OEM-standard parts)", "Worldwide shipping", "Catalog management for 25,000+ SKUs"], "industries": ["Classic automotive restoration", "Automotive aftermarket parts distribution", "Counterpart Automotive", "Fargo Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Most in-stock items ship quickly", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 25,000 parts in stock for classic Chevy and GMC vehicles", "Technical support from experienced restoration professionals", "Fast shipping on most in-stock items", "Family-owned and operated by classic car enthusiasts", "Modern upgrades (hidden radios, A/C) that integrate with vintage interiors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db", "Headquarters Bentonville, Arkansas -> db", "Family-owned business -> page /", "Over 25,000 parts in inventory -> page /", "Specializes in classic Chevy and GMC vehicles 1955-1987 -> page /", "Technical support from experienced restoration professionals -> page /", "Fast shipping on in-stock items -> page /", "Worldwide shipping -> page /", "Quality assurance meets or exceeds OEM standards -> page /", "Modern upgrades like hidden radios and A/C -> page /", "Brands carried: Cold Case Radiators, Dakota Digital, NU-Relics Power Windows, Vintage Air -> page /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Today, H&H is one of the largest online retailers of classic car restoration parts", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='h-h-classic-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1998, H&R Steel Supplies and Fabrication has operated as a family-owned and operated retail steel and fabrication business in Spartanburg, South Carolina, for over two decades. The company was established to provide the local community with a full line of metal products and processing services.

The shop maintains hundreds of stock items in carbon steel, aluminum, and stainless steel, offered in standard 10-, 12-, 20-, and 24-foot lengths that can be cut to exact project requirements. In-house processing equipment includes an iron worker, band saw, drill press, metal shear, bender, mill, and punch, supporting cutting, shearing, bending, milling, and punching operations. Fabrication services cover MIG, TIG, and stick welding with extensive experience in aluminum, steel, and stainless steel.

The facility is open to the public six days a week and serves walk-in retail customers, local contractors, and small businesses across the Spartanburg region. Materials are sold by the foot, and a selection of drop pieces is available for smaller jobs.

