UPDATE companies SET description='Hansen International, Inc. is headquartered in Lexington, South Carolina, where it has operated since consolidating its manufacturing facilities in 2003. The company traces its roots to 1920 when A.L. "Auggie" Hansen, a Danish immigrant who had worked with Thomas Edison during World War I, founded the business in Chicago. Now in its fourth generation of family ownership, the firm is led by President Lisa Beebe, who assumed the role in 2017.

The company engineers, manufactures, and globally sources commercial and industrial vehicle hardware and trim systems. Its 110,000-square-foot Lexington plant houses assembly, on-site painting, on-site quality testing, stamping, and welding operations. Hansen also provides inventory management, EDI, just-in-time and Kanban supply chain services, custom packaging, and prototype development, supporting both short-run and production volumes.

