UPDATE companies SET description='Hawaii Solar Outfitters operates from Pāhoa on the Big Island of Hawaii. Founder Tim Heltzel launched the company after a decade of solar installation experience in East Hawaii, driven by frustration with large firms that priced out homeowners and forced them through lengthy utility interconnection queues and county permitting processes. The business remains a sole proprietorship with no sales staff or commissioned representatives.

The company designs and installs off-grid and grid-tied solar power systems, specializing in off-grid configurations that avoid HELCO interconnection requirements. Heltzel personally handles every project — from system sizing and component selection to installation and follow-up. Typical installations use SUNKET 430W UL-listed solar panels, EG4 hybrid inverters, and EG4 LiFePO4 battery storage sized for Hawaii''s climate. A free off-grid health check includes real-world battery load testing and full site analysis.

Hawaii Solar Outfitters serves residential customers across East Hawaii, including Hilo, Keaau, Pahoa, Mountain View, Fern Forest, Fern Acres, and Volcano. Projects range from basic cabin systems starting around $10,000 to full homestead installations with heavy loads such as air conditioning and well pumps. The installer also works with existing off-grid systems that suffer from excessive generator run-time or battery degradation.

Heltzel emphasizes direct accountability: the same person who designs the system installs it and returns for any service needs. Components are chosen based on real-world testing in local conditions rather than specifications alone. By eliminating sales commissions and permitting delays for off-grid builds, the company aims to deliver energy independence faster and at lower cost than conventional solar contractors.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Off-grid solar system design", "Off-grid solar system installation", "Grid-tied solar system installation", "Off-grid system health check (battery load testing, site analysis)", "System sizing and component selection", "Real-world load testing"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Off-grid power systems", "Renewable energy installation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SUNKET 430W solar panels", "EG4 hybrid inverters", "EG4 LiFePO4 battery storage"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No utility interconnection queue or county permitting delays for off-grid systems", "Free off-grid system health check with real load testing, not guesswork", "Direct accountability \u2014 no sales teams, commissions, or middlemen", "Components selected after real-world testing in Hawaii''s climate", "Single point of contact from design through installation and service"], "facts_used": ["Founder Tim Heltzel -> /", "Location P\u0101hoa, Hawaii -> /", "10 years solar installation experience -> /", "Sole proprietorship, no sales team -> /", "Services: off-grid and grid-tied solar installation -> /", "Free off-grid health check with real load testing -> /", "Components: SUNKET 430W panels, EG4 inverters, EG4 LiFePO4 batteries -> /", "Service areas: Hilo, Keaau, Pahoa, Mountain View, Fern Forest, Fern Acres, Volcano -> /", "Certification UL Listed -> db", "Pricing ranges for system tiers -> /", "No HELCO interconnection queue or permitting delays for off-grid -> /", "Direct accountability, same person for design/install/service -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "I handle every job myself \u2014 design, install, and follow-up.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "1", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hawaii-solar-outfitters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Hawaii Spring Supply Inc operates from two locations in Honolulu and Hilo, Hawaii. Founded in 1956, the company has remained a family-owned, locally operated business for over six decades. It identifies as an Asian-owned small business.

The company stocks a large inventory of truck and trailer parts, including suspension components, brakes, clutches, air valves, hitches, tires, wheels, and driveshafts. It also builds custom driveshafts and provides fabrication services for automotive parts. The shop is noted as the last certified spring shop in the state. Services include lighting services, same-day delivery, and pickup/delivery options.

It is associated with Power Heavy Duty and the National Association of Trailer Manufacturers (NATM).

