UPDATE companies SET description='The company remains a fourth-generation family-owned business; its origins trace to 1957 when William A. LeBouef Sr., great-grandfather of current owner Sara Bell, invented a continuous roll-forming system that earned U.S. Patent No. 3,009,511 in 1961.

It runs its own roll-forming equipment — custom-cut roll-form machines based on the patented process — and uses high-tensile steel. Over eight decades it has sold more than 65,000 buildings and shipped over 75 million tons of metal.

Hercules serves commercial, industrial, and residential construction markets. Its building kits have been used for commercial garages, industrial warehouses, farm structures, prefabricated industrial facilities, pre-engineered workshops, sports arenas, office buildings, airplane hangars, self-storage units, cannabis cultivation facilities, and remote mining buildings.

