UPDATE companies SET description='High Speed Interconnect LLC (HSI) was formed in December 2010 in Scottsdale, Arizona. The company quickly expanded through strategic acquisitions of Riverview Custom Cable and ESM Cable Corp in early 2011, then invested in coaxial cable extrusion and fine‑wire termination platforms. Corporate leadership and administration remain in Scottsdale, while manufacturing is conducted in two centers in Tigard, Oregon and Hermosillo, Mexico.

HSI extrudes its own high‑performance coaxial cable using solid, foamed, and expanded PTFE (VP90) dielectrics, and assembles cable assemblies ranging from 16 to 52 AWG. Configurations include single coax, twinax, triax, quadax, shielded parallel and twisted pairs, and multi‑conductor constructions in discrete, ribbonized, or bundled forms. The company manages nearly all critical processes in‑house — extrusion, termination, testing — and serves over 200 OEM and government‑agency customers.

Its customer base includes OEMs, government agencies, and universities. HSI is factory certified to terminate Hirose, IPEX, and JAE micro‑coaxial connectors, and its quality systems comply with AS9100D, ISO 13485, and ITAR requirements.

HSI differentiates itself by controlling nearly all critical technologies and processes internally to eliminate tradeoffs in insertion loss, phase stability, capacitance, and velocity of propagation. The company also emphasizes no minimum order requirements and lead times that range from 24 hours to eight weeks.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 13485:2016','ITAR Registered','RoHS 2011/65/EU','IPC-610','IPC-620','MIL-I-45208','Hirose Certified','IPEX Certified','JAE Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coaxial cable extrusion", "Expanded PTFE (ePTFE/VP90) extrusion", "Fine wire termination (down to 0.175 mm)", "Direct-to-board termination", "Micro coaxial cable assembly (30-52 AWG)", "Coaxial cable assembly (16-29 AWG)", "Multi-conductor cable assembly (discrete, ribbonized, bundled)", "Impedance-matched cable assembly (50 \u03a9, 100 \u03a9 differential)", "Connector termination (Hirose, IPEX, JAE certified)", "New Product Introduction (NPI) support", "Legacy product transfer", "Engineering design and simulation", "IPC-610/620 certified assembly", "ITAR-compliant manufacturing", "Conflict minerals compliance", "RoHS compliance"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Medical Devices", "Telecommunications", "Research & Education"], "materials": ["PTFE (solid, foamed, expanded)", "Expanded PTFE (VP90)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "24 hours to 8 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manages nearly all critical technologies and processes in-house", "No minimum order requirements", "Lead times from 24 hours to 8 weeks", "Extrudes its own high-performance coaxial cable and expanded PTFE (VP90)", "Factory certified for Hirose, IPEX, and JAE micro-coaxial connectors"], "facts_used": ["Founded December 2010 -> /about", "Headquarters Scottsdale, AZ -> /about, /, db", "Acquisitions of Riverview Custom Cable and ESM Cable Corp Jan/Feb 2011 -> /about", "Manufacturing centers in Tigard, OR and Hermosillo, MX -> /about", "Over 200 OEM and gov