UPDATE companies SET description='Hy-Ten Plastics Inc operates from its headquarters and production facility in Milford, New Hampshire. The company has served the medical, electronic, industrial, and consumer industries for 60 years, specializing in tight-tolerance plastic injection molding and related value-added services. Ownership details and founder names are not disclosed in the available information.

Hy-Ten provides full-service custom injection molding, from design and engineering through tooling, prototyping, and production. Its Milford facility houses 22 electric injection molding machines ranging from 55 to 385 tons, a certified Class 8 cleanroom, and a 3D CMM scanner for reverse engineering. The company offers scientific molding methodology, mold flow simulation, and 3D production prototyping via fused deposition modeling (FDM) with five material options. Value-added services include ultrasonic welding, machining, drilling and tapping, plating, printing, painting, custom packaging, barcoding, and vendor-managed inventory. Hy-Ten has produced millions of complex disposable medical parts and supports volumes from prototype to high-volume manufacturing.

Hy-Ten serves medical, electronic, industrial, and consumer markets. Medical customers include manufacturers of blood filtration devices, IV drip valves, and complex disposable assemblies. Electronic applications encompass hand-held printer assemblies, electronic and chemical analyzers, and wireless communication housings. Industrial projects have addressed molded-in bearings, thick-walled parts, and filtration system components.

Hy-Ten emphasizes in-house management of all services from design through manufacturing to control cost, quality, and lead times. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016. The company cites a culture of integrity, respect, and quality, with a focus on customer partnerships, continuous improvement, and business ethics as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Injection Molding", "Tight Tolerance Molding", "Design & Engineering", "Mold Flow Simulation", "File Conversion (SolidWorks, Mastercam)", "3D Prototyping (FDM)", "Scientific Molding", "Tooling (Mold Making & Design)", "Clean Room Molding (Class 8)", "Insert Molding", "Assembly", "Ultrasonic Welding", "Machining & Drilling/Tapping", "Plating & Decorative Services (Printing, Painting)", "Custom Packaging, Barcoding & Vendor Managed Inventory", "Process Validations", "PPAP", "FAI", "DOE", "Metrology Studies (Cpk, Ppk)", "Reverse Engineering (3D CMM Scanning)", "Annealing"], "industries": ["Medical", "Electronic", "Industrial", "Consumer"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["22 Electric Injection Molding Machines (55\u2013385 ton)", "3D CMM Scanner (reverse engineering)", "Annealing Oven", "Mold Flow Simulation Software", "SolidWorks", "Mastercam", "Tool Vault (environmentally controlled, integrated asset management)", "FDM 3D Printer"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume manufacturing", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["22 electric injection molding machines (55\u2013385 ton)", "Certified Class 8 cleanroom for medical molding", "In-house design, tooling, and molding under one roof", "Scientific molding methodology with documented process validation", "3D production prototyping (FDM) with five material options"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters and production facility in Milford, NH -> /", "Served medical, electronic, industrial, consumer industries for 60 years -> /", "Specializes in tight-