UPDATE companies SET description='Illinois Components, Inc. was founded in 1996 in Lombard, Illinois, by Tony and Keith Bondi, who serve as president and vice president respectively. The company began as a specialist in tape and reel services, focusing on surface mount taping for automated electronics assembly.

The firm provides a range of packaging and programming services for electronic components. Its core offerings include surface mount taping, radial and axial taping, tape and reel packaging, electronic component programming, cut and form operations, and inspection. Work is performed in a clean, modern facility using high-speed automated equipment that handles tape widths from 8 to 120 mm and reel diameters of 7, 13, 15, and 22 inches. The company also supplies metal stampings, spacers, and standoffs for the metals industry and offers custom carrier pocket designs and barcoded labeling.

Illinois Components serves the electronics manufacturing sector, handling all surface mount and through-hole devices, as well as the metals industry for spacers, stampings, screw-machine parts, and standoffs. Its customers are typically original equipment manufacturers and contract assemblers seeking to streamline production with reliable, standards-compliant packaging.

The company emphasizes rapid turnaround, quoting completion from inception to delivery in one week or less for custom solutions. It adheres to EIA taping standards and ESD procedures, and differentiates itself through custom pocket design, quick-turn programming, and a customer-centric approach that prioritizes precision and on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface mount taping", "Radial taping", "Axial taping", "Tape and reel packaging", "Electronic component programming", "Cut and form", "Inspection", "Custom carrier pocket design", "Custom barcoded labeling", "Metal stampings supply", "Metal spacers supply", "Standoffs supply"], "industries": ["Electronics manufacturing", "Metals fabrication"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "One week or less for custom solutions; rapid turn-around for standard services", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom carrier pocket design for unique components", "Turnaround from inception to completion in one week or less", "High-speed automated taping equipment handling 8\u2013120 mm tape widths", "Compliance with EIA taping standards and ESD procedures", "Custom barcoded labeling on reels"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 in Lombard, Illinois -> db", "Founders Tony Bondi (President) and Keith Bondi (Vice President) -> /", "Services: surface mount taping, radial/axial taping, tape and reel, programming, cut and form, inspection -> /", "Equipment: high-speed automated machines, tape widths 8-120mm, reel sizes 7/13/15/22 inch -> /", "Standards: EIA taping standards, ESD procedures -> /", "Industries: electronics (SMT and through-hole), metals (spacers, stampings, screw machines, standoffs) -> /", "Turnaround: one week or less for custom solutions -> /", "Custom carrier pocket design and barcoded labeling -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1996, Illinois Components, Inc. has proudly served as a trusted provider of tape and reel services, with a specialization in surface mount taping.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='illinois-components' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Imperium Cable LLC is a U.S. company headquartered in Troy, Michigan, serving the North American commercial, industrial, solar, and residential markets. The company sells its products through an electrical distribution network supported by a roster of manufacturers’ representatives covering most of the United States.

Its product line spans low- and medium-voltage cables in single- and multi-conductor configurations, using copper or aluminum conductors with thermoplastic or thermosetting insulation (XLP/EPR) and jackets of PVC, PE, CPE, or cross-linked materials. Medium-voltage cables are tested to AEIC requirements and certified by a independent high-voltage laboratory.

The commercial segment targets hotels, offices, hospitals, schools, shopping centers, mixed-use communities, underground parking garages, and apartments. The industrial segment addresses wastewater treatment plants, petrochemical facilities, pulp and paper mills, pharmaceutical plants, oil and gas operations, mining, and marine applications. Residential offerings include NM-B nonmetallic sheathed cable, while the solar line provides UL-listed PV wire in copper and aluminum at 600 V and 2000 V ratings.

The company emphasizes the breadth of its product line, the scale and certification of its manufacturing footprint, and the third-party validation of its medium-voltage cables as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9000','ISO 14000','OHSAS 18001','UL Listed','AEIC qualification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Building wire manufacturing (THHN/THWN-2, XHHW-2, THW)", "Metal-clad (MC) cable manufacturing", "Nonmetallic sheathed cable (NM-B) manufacturing", "Medium voltage power cable manufacturing (MV-90, MV-105)", "Tray cable manufacturing (XLP, THHN, EPR)", "Armored cable manufacturing (Type MC, MC-HL)", "Portable power cable manufacturing (SOOW, DLO, Type W, G, G-GC)", "Mining cable manufacturing (SHD-GC, Mine Power Feeder)", "Solar photovoltaic wire manufacturing (PV XLPE)"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Residential", "Solar"], "materials": ["Copper", "Aluminum", "Thermoplastic", "Thermosetting (XLP/EPR)", "Polyethylene (PE)", "Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC)", "Chlorinated Polyethylene (CPE)", "Cross-linked jacket coverings"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Medium-voltage cables qualified to AEIC standards and certified by a top independent high-voltage lab", "Comprehensive product line covering commercial, industrial, residential, and solar applications", "Products meet or exceed U.S. industry standards and are UL listed", "Nationwide sales network of manufacturers\u2019 representatives"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Troy, Michigan -> /", "Manufacturing facilities totaling 2,400,000 sq ft -> /", "Facilities certified ISO 9000, ISO 14000, OHSAS 18001 -> /", "Medium voltage cables tested to AEIC requirements and certified by independent lab -> /", "Product lines: commercial, industrial, residential, solar -> /", "Commercial applications: hotels, offices, hospitals, schools, shopping centers, mixed-use, underground parking, apartments -> /", "Industrial applications: wastewater, petrochemical, pulp & paper, pharmaceutical, oil & gas, mining, marine -> /", "Residential product: NM-B copper conductor 600V -> /", "Solar product: PV XLPE copper/aluminum 600V and 2000V -> /", "Sales through electrical distribution network with manufacturers'' representatives -> /", "Certifications: UL Listed -> db", "HQ city: Troy, state: Michigan -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturing facilities totaling 2,400,000 square feet are utilized to produce Imperium Cable\u2019s product line", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='imperium-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='In Style USA was founded in 2013 in New York City’s Garment District by Tina Yu, a designer and patternmaker from a multi-generational fashion manufacturing family. After launching her own eveningwear collection in Toronto, Yu relocated to New York and established the atelier, which quickly attracted clients such as Bill Blass and Oscar de la Renta. James Mallon, a veteran of Oxford Industries and former label owner, later joined as a partner, adding global sourcing expertise.

The company provides full-package garment development and production from a roughly 10,000-square-foot facility housing more than 60 sewing machines and two on-site cutting tables. Services span product review and consultation, fabric and trim sourcing, pattern making, garment fitting, sample making, product development, resource guidance, sewing and hand sewing, production management, packaging, and design and branding. The vertical operation moves designs from concept through bulk production under one roof.

In Style USA serves fashion designers and apparel brands ranging from established houses to emerging labels. Its client roster has included names like Bill Blass and Oscar de la Renta, and its garments are sold at top retail accounts worldwide. The firm has been a member of the Council of Fashion Designers of America since 2013 and was the inaugural recipient of the Fashion Manufacturing Initiative grant, a program backed by the CFDA and the New York City Economic Development Corporation.

