UPDATE companies SET description='Inglot Electronics Corporation, based in Chicago, Illinois, was founded in 1964 by Peter Inglot, who arrived in the United States in 1955 with the ambition of establishing his own company. The business remains headquartered in Chicago, where a workforce of approximately 30 employees operates under the guiding principles of respect, pride, and dedication established by its founder.

The company designs and manufactures a broad range of custom electro‑magnetic components for power conversion, including linear laminated transformers (rated from 22 kVA to 100 MVA), miniature toroids, switch‑mode magnetics, high‑ and low‑frequency power chokes, linear transformers, and solenoid coils. Its service portfolio covers design engineering, prototype testing, paper‑section layer winding, computerized three‑axis winding, toroidal assembly, in‑process inspection, and computerized final testing, with optional special testing, data reporting, and bar‑coding.

Inglot serves customers in the power‑conversion industry and, following the 2005 acquisition of Associated Transformer, the military sector. The company cites partnerships with several Fortune 500 firms, both domestic and international, as evidence of its ability to meet tight design specifications, just‑in‑time delivery schedules, and competitive pricing demands.

Management emphasizes a “Made in the USA” production model, scheduling flexibility, and a culture rooted in the founder’s values of respect, pride, and dedication. These factors, combined with engineering expertise in VDE, CSA, UL, and BSI standards, are presented as the basis for the company’s reputation for quality and reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['VDE','CSA','UL','BSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design engineering", "Prototype testing", "Paper section layerwinding", "Computerized 3-axis winding", "Toroidal assembly", "In-process inspection", "Computerized final testing", "Special testing", "Data reporting", "Bar coding", "Custom electromagnetic component design", "Custom electromagnetic component manufacturing"], "industries": ["Power conversion", "Military", "Magnetics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["JIT delivery capability", "Tight design expertise", "Made in the USA manufacturing", "Special testing, data reporting, and bar coding available", "Scheduling flexibility"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1964 -> /about", "Headquarters Chicago, Illinois -> /", "Founder Peter Inglot arrived 1955 -> /", "30 employees -> /", "Manufactures linear laminated transformers 22 kVA to 100 MVA -> /about", "Manufactures miniature toroids, switch mode magnetics, power chokes, linear transformers, solenoid coils -> /about", "Services: design engineering, prototype testing, paper section layerwinding, computerized 3-axis winding, toroidal assembly, in-process inspection, computerized final testing -> /services", "Special testing, data reporting, bar coding available -> /about", "Acquisitions: Ex-Qual Transformer (2001), Nelco Coil Supply (2003), Associated Transformer (2005) -> /about", "Partnerships with Fortune 500 customers -> /about", "Engineers specialists in VDE, CSA, UL, BSI -> /", "Made in the USA -> /", "JIT delivery, tight design capabilities -> /about", "Principles of respect, pride, dedication -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we manufacture miniature toroids, switch mode magnetics, high and low frequency power chokes, linear transformers, and solenoid coils", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "30", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/inglot-electronics-corporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='inglot-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='InnoSys Inc. was founded in 2000 and operates from a facility near downtown Salt Lake City, Utah. The company began as a developer of advanced electronic devices and subsystems, leveraging expertise in microelectronics and materials science.

The company provides integrated manufacturing services spanning micro-fabrication, MEMS, micro-machining, 3D ceramic printing, electronic packaging, and extensive test and evaluation. Its Salt Lake City site includes a Class 1000 cleanroom, brazing chambers, machining equipment, and assembly lines, allowing production from starting materials to finished packages.

InnoSys serves aerospace, vacuum electronics, solid-state lighting, and microelectronics sectors. Its solid-state vacuum devices (SSVDs) have been presented at the IEEE Aerospace Conference and International Vacuum Electronics Conference, while its OLED power supply work has been featured in Department of Energy workshops and OLED stakeholder meetings.

