UPDATE companies SET description='Intermountain Wind & Solar was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in Centerville, Utah. The company serves the Intermountain West region, including Utah, Idaho, Wyoming, and Oregon, providing solar power solutions for homes, businesses, and government facilities.

The company designs and installs custom solar panel and battery backup systems, handling every step from system design and permitting to installation and ongoing maintenance. All electricians and installers are full-time employees rather than subcontractors. Intermountain Wind & Solar works with name-brand equipment such as Hyundai, Trina, and mSolar panels; Enphase and SolarEdge inverters; and Tesla Powerwall batteries. The firm also offers flexible financing options to reduce upfront costs. It reports thousands of installations completed across its service territory.

Customers include residential homeowners in cities like Salt Lake City, ranch owners in Wyoming, and commercial facilities in Boise, as well as government projects. The company tailors systems to withstand the region’s intense winds, heavy snow, and temperature swings.

Intermountain Wind & Solar says its differentiation comes from not outsourcing labor, bulk purchasing that enables low per-watt pricing, and deep local knowledge of state incentives and weather challenges. Its stated mission is to be the premiere provider of custom solar power solutions, guided by values including integrity, honesty, professionalism, accountability, hard work, and communication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar system design", "Permitting and paperwork management", "Solar panel installation", "Battery backup system installation", "System maintenance and support", "Solar financing options", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Government solar projects", "EV charging station installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Government", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Hyundai solar panels", "Trina solar panels", "mSolar solar panels", "Enphase inverters", "SolarEdge inverters", "Tesla Powerwall batteries"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All installations performed by full-time employee electricians and installers, no subcontractors", "Bulk equipment purchasing passes savings to customers for some of the lowest per-watt pricing in the region", "Systems custom-designed for high winds, heavy snow, and extreme temperature swings", "Only trusted, name-brand equipment installed (Hyundai, Trina, mSolar, Enphase, SolarEdge, Tesla Powerwall)", "Flexible financing options available"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 -> db", "Headquartered in Centerville, Utah -> db", "Serves Utah, Idaho, Wyoming, Oregon -> /", "Does not outsource installations; full-time employees -> /quality, /", "Installs Hyundai, Trina, mSolar panels; Enphase, SolarEdge inverters; Tesla Powerwall batteries -> /", "Offers flexible financing options -> /", "Thousands of installations completed -> /", "Over a decade of experience -> /", "Mission: Be the premiere provider of custom solar power solutions -> /", "Values: Integrity, Honesty, Professionalism, Accountability, Hard-work, Communication -> /", "Serves residential, commercial, government -> /", "Custom designs for high winds, snow, temperature swings -> /", "Bulk purchasing for low per-watt pricing -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We do not outsource our installations. All of our electricians and installers are full-time IWS employees (not independent contractors) that install solar all day, every day.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='intermountain-wind-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company began as a focused magnetics provider and later expanded into larger facilities in nearby Brockton before settling at its current mailing address in South Easton.

Today the firm designs and builds a range of power conversion products, including isolated and non‑isolated DC‑DC converters from 1 W to 150 W, AC‑DC power supplies, and custom transformers and inductors. In addition to its own magnetics line, International Coil has formed engineering alliances with partners such as ALFA, LLC for analog hardware and power conversion, Bartek Technologies for firmware and FPGA development, Avanti Design & Development for mechanical and thermal modeling, and rfLyncs for RF and antenna design covering Wi‑Fi, Bluetooth, Zigbee, LoRa, RFID, cellular and GPS. These partnerships extend the company’s capabilities into full‑system wireless hardware, regulatory compliance (FCC Part 15, CTIA, SAR), and design‑for‑manufacturing support.

The company serves customers in power electronics, wireless communications, and defense‑related programs, as evidenced by its ITAR registration. Typical engagements include custom magnetic designs for OEM power supplies, wireless module development for portable and wearable devices, and engineering support for products requiring UL certification and RoHS compliance.

International Coil emphasizes on‑time delivery, competitive pricing, and engineering expertise as its primary differentiators. The company states that it was started to provide cost‑effective, reliable transformers and coils, and it now promotes a combination of custom design capability, quality assurance under ISO 9001:2015, and responsive customer service.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','UL (OBJY2.E176555)','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power supply design and manufacturing (1W-150W)", "DC-DC converter manufacturing (isolated and non-isolated)", "AC-DC power supply manufacturing", "Transformer and inductor manufacturing", "Custom magnetic design", "Analog hardware design", "Power conversion design", "Electro-optics design", "Signal integrity/power integrity PCB analysis", "Digital design (firmware, embedded control, FPGA, DSP)", "Mechanical and electro-mechanical design", "Design for manufacturing and assembly (DFM/DFA)", "RF and antenna design", "Wireless hardware design (WiFi, BT, Zigbee, LoRa, RFID, cellular, GPS)", "Custom antenna design", "Regulatory compliance (FCC Part 15, CTIA, SAR)", "ITAR compliance", "ISO 9001:2015 quality management", "UL certification (OBJY2.E176555)", "RoHS compliance"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-time shipping commitment", "Competitive pricing", "Engineering expertise through partner alliances", "ITAR registered and ISO 9001:2015 certified", "Custom design capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1995 -> db", "Headquarters in South Easton, MA -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "UL certified (OBJY2.E176555) -> /", "RoHS compliant -> /", "Manufactures power supplies, DC-DC converters, transformers, inductors -> /", "Engineering alliances with ALFA, Bartek Technologies, Avanti Design & Development, rfLyncs -> /", "Custom design capability -> /", "On-time shipping, competitive pricing, engineering expertise, quality, customer service claimed -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "International Coil Inc. was founded in 1995 to provide manufactured products and services to customers needing cost effective and reliable transformers and coils.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='international-coil-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1957 as Interstate – GM Diesel in Minneapolis, Minnesota, the company began as one of the first distributors for Detroit Diesel and Allison Transmission. Now operating as Interstate Power Systems, the business is headquartered in Gillette, Wyoming, and maintains a network of locations across twelve Midwestern and Western states.

The company distributes on-highway and off-highway engines and transmissions and provides a full range of support services. Its Gillette facility offers generator sales and service, contract maintenance, electrical load bank testing, electric motor and radiator repair, crane and construction equipment repair, and mining equipment assembly and disassembly. Technicians also handle transport refrigeration, light utility vehicles, and dielectric testing, with 24/7 emergency response available.

Interstate serves customers in oil and gas, mining, construction, industrial manufacturing, transportation, power generation, and marine sectors. Vocational truck fleets, heavy equipment operators, and mining operations rely on its OEM parts inventory and field service crews to minimize downtime.

