UPDATE companies SET description='J & C Wood Products operates from Plaucheville, Louisiana, a town of roughly 288 residents. The company was founded in 2001 by Jody and Candace Chenevert, who brought over 25 years of hardwood industry experience to the venture. Starting from humble beginnings, the couple built a business focused on reclaimed and specialty wood products.

The company mills solid wood flooring from reclaimed antique heart pine, white oak, hickory/pecan, and hemlock, as well as producing beams, table tops, counter tops, stair treads, mantles, doors, cabinets, charcuterie boards, and pre-finished engineered flooring. A key process is thermally modified kiln drying, where wood is heated above 180°C in an oxygen-free environment for up to five days to enhance durability without chemicals. Reclaimed beams are sourced from antique structures across the United States and milled to custom dimensions. The operation includes a showroom at its new mill facility.

J & C serves both commercial and residential markets, supplying flooring and beams to homeowners, builders, and designers. Its products have been featured in Design & Build Magazine of Southwest Louisiana, and customer testimonials reference projects in Arkansas, Louisiana, and New Orleans.

The Cheneverts emphasize old-world craftsmanship, positioning their La Olden brand as ultra-premium unfinished flooring made in the traditions of traditional artisans. The thermally modified wood line is promoted as a sustainable, chemical-free option for outdoor applications with a lifespan of 25 to 50 years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid wood flooring milling", "Reclaimed wood processing", "Thermally modified wood kiln drying", "Beam reclamation and milling", "Custom mantle milling", "Table and counter top fabrication", "Stair tread manufacturing", "Door and cabinet making", "Charcuterie board production", "Pre-finished engineered wood flooring production", "Flooring installation"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Antique reclaimed heart pine", "White oak", "Hickory", "Pecan", "Hemlock", "Thermally modified wood"], "equipment": ["Thermally modified wood kiln", "Sawmill/milling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Thermally modified kiln drying process (up to 5 days, no chemical additives)", "Reclaimed beams sourced from antique structures nationwide", "Tongue-and-groove milling for uniform thickness", "Old-world craftsmanship traditions", "Showroom at new mill facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters in Plaucheville, Louisiana -> db", "Founders Jody and Candace Chenevert with over 25 years experience -> /", "Produces solid wood flooring from reclaimed antique heart pine, white oak, hickory/pecan, hemlock -> /", "Offers thermally modified kiln dried wood process (>180\u00b0C, oxygen-free, up to 5 days) -> /", "Reclaims beams from antique structures across the United States -> /", "Manufactures beams, table tops, counter tops, stair treads, mantles, doors, cabinets, charcuterie boards, pre-finished engineered flooring -> /", "Has showroom at new mill -> /", "Serves commercial and residential markets -> /", "Featured in Design & Build Magazine of Southwest Louisiana -> /", "Provides installation services -> /", "La Olden brand emphasizes old-world craftsmanship -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "J&C Wood Products & Laolden Flooring creates ultra-premium, unfinished solid antique reclaimed heart pine, white oak, hickory/pecan, & hemlock flooring along with beams and other accessories in the traditions of old-world craftsmen.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-c-wood-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J Custom Supply, Inc. was founded in 1979 in Zachary, Louisiana, by Jason Fendelson to provide stage lighting and power distribution equipment for the touring production Holiday on Ice. The company relocated to Baton Rouge in 2005 when Fendelson retired and Charles "Gil" Gilliam assumed ownership.

The company stocks and supplies a broad range of cam-style connectors, including Crouse-Hinds Cam-Lok and Marinco CAM Technology lines, along with generator connection boxes, test clamps, and front-of-house power panels. It maintains one of the largest inventories of cam connectors in the southeastern United States, with most items available for immediate shipment.

J Custom Supply serves the theater, entertainment, and emergency portable power sectors. Its customer base spans local bands and venues to major convention centers and generator rental firms across nearly every U.S. state and Puerto Rico, with international clients in Canada, Saudi Arabia, Korea, Hong Kong, the United Kingdom, Taiwan, India, Singapore, and the Bahamas. Notable accounts include Boeing, Feld Entertainment, Caterpillar, BAE Systems, and Mercedes-Benz.

